# HotFox V5 visual law

- UI is NOT visually accepted at V4: 18/18 captures exist but 0/18 pass.
- Read `verification/ui_rebuild/HOTFOX_ART_DIRECTOR_REVIEW_FAIL_V5.md` and `design/HOTFOX_CURSOR_ART_DIRECTOR_REFINEMENT_V5.txt`.
- Asset kit is a parts bin, not automatic visual truth.
- Never use decorative planet, planetary arc, eclipse, celestial horizon, closed orbit rings, solar-system composition, or radar-like concentric orbital systems.
- V5 extends this prohibition to current AUTO/Ready illustrations if they visually read as orbital systems.
- Fox artwork must not show an opaque rectangular matte. Use a clean transparent fox asset; fox interior must remain opaque, feather only outer silhouette.
- Do not repeat the broken semi-transparent dark-fur alpha extraction.
- Production truth and debug visual reference state are separate. Debug fixtures under src/debug are allowed and encouraged for visual QA of reference-populated states.
- Never leak fixture servers, subscription, apps, traffic, latency, entitlement or CONNECTED state into release.
- Production CONNECTED/Защищено remains gated by real readiness.
- Use reference-state fixtures for 10/11/12/15 when approved board needs populated data.
- Do not use one full-width orange pill CTA mechanically on every screen.
- Content-over-containers remains required, but raw unstructured lists are also not acceptable; use subtle editorial grouping.
- Typography, spacing and headers must be measured per screen.
- No dead/unfinished lower-half layout unless reference intentionally uses that negative space.
- All 18 V5 screenshots and comparisons are mandatory.
- V4 evidence must be preserved; write V5 evidence to new directories/files.
- Do not merge.
- RELEASE READY is a separate runtime gate.
